+### Strict Parsing
+
+Pass `{ strict: true }` to throw an `Error` containing the input when a string
+cannot be parsed, including strings longer than 100 characters. Only literal
+`true` enables strict mode. By default, unparseable strings return `undefined`.
+
+```js
+ms('2 days', { strict: true }) // 172800000
+ms('invalid')                 // undefined
+ms('invalid', { strict: true }) // throws Error: Unable to parse time string. val="invalid"
+```
+
+Strict mode does not affect numeric formatting. Empty strings and invalid input
+types continue to throw regardless of the strict option.
